            <ArticleTitle>Intertrochanteric fracture non-unions with implant failure of the gamma nail.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>57</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.11604/pamj.2016.23.57.7965</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Failure of internal fixation of intertrochanteric fracture is associated with delayed union or malunion resulting in persistent pain and diminished function. We report a rare case of implant failure of the gamma nail with intertrochanteric fracture non union treated by DCS plate screw and bone graft.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
